<?php declare(strict_types=1); ?><!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><meta name="description" content="Trust-Worthy traces claims to evidence, separates fact from inference, and shows what survives investigation."><title>Trust-Worthy | Evidence Desk</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/truth/truth-worthy.css"></head><body><header class="topbar"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/truth/">TRUST-WORTHY <span>EVIDENCE DESK</span></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="#investigate">Investigate</a><a href="#featured">Case Desk</a><a href="#trials">Case Files</a><a href="/truth/lab/">Evidence Lab</a><a href="/book/research.html">Standards</a></nav></div></header><main><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT UNVEILED // TRUST-WORTHY // OPEN EVIDENCE SYSTEM</div><h1>DON'T TRUST US.<br>CHECK THE EVIDENCE.</h1><p>Drop in a claim. Trust-Worthy traces where it came from, tests competing explanations, separates verified facts from inference and missing context, and shows you what the evidence actually supports.</p><div class="manifesto"><strong>No protected conclusions.</strong> No side gets a free pass. We show our work. <strong>You be the judge.</strong></div><div class="desk-strip"><div class="desk-stat"><strong>INPUT</strong><span>Claim · URL · Post</span></div><div class="desk-stat"><strong>PROCESS</strong><span>Trace · Test · Challenge</span></div><div class="desk-stat"><strong>OUTPUT</strong><span>Evidence · Unknowns</span></div><div class="desk-stat"><strong>STANDARD</strong><span>Revise when evidence wins</span></div></div></div></section><section class="section" id="investigate"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card daily-desk"><div class="eyebrow">NEW INVESTIGATION // INTAKE TERMINAL</div><h2>What do you want investigated?</h2><p>Paste a Facebook post, headline, claim, URL, or statement. The free trial produces a concise AI-assisted preliminary analysis; source-authenticated Deep Dives remain a separate evidentiary level.</p><form class="challenge" action="/truth/investigate.php" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="opened_at" id="questionOpenedAt" value=""><div class="hp" aria-hidden="true"><label>Website<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></div><label for="question">CLAIM / QUESTION / POST</label><textarea id="question" name="question" minlength="20" maxlength="3000" required placeholder="Paste the claim exactly as you received it. Include context when available..."></textarea><button class="button" type="submit">RUN INVESTIGATION →</button><p><small>Read the <a href="/privacy.html#free-truth-trial-privacy">privacy boundary</a> before starting. Preliminary trials are not substitutes for authenticated primary-source research.</small></p></form></article><aside class="card"><div class="eyebrow">ANALYST PROTOCOL</div><h2>What gets separated.</h2><ul class="rules"><li><strong>Verified fact</strong> — directly supported by reliable evidence.</li><li><strong>Inference</strong> — a conclusion drawn from facts, not the fact itself.</li><li><strong>Missing context</strong> — material information that changes interpretation.</li><li><strong>Disputed</strong> — credible evidence or authorities materially disagree.</li><li><strong>Unknown</strong> — the available evidence cannot responsibly settle it.</li></ul><div class="finding"><strong>Core rule:</strong> A true fact can still create a misleading narrative when selection, omission, or framing pushes the reader beyond what the evidence establishes.</div></aside></div></section><section class="section" id="featured"><div class="wrap"><article class="card daily-desk"><div class="eyebrow">FEATURED CASE FILE // TW-000004</div><div class="case-head"><div><h2>Did the CIA control the American media?</h2></div><div class="verdict">DOCUMENTED ACTIVITY / BROADER CLAIM UNPROVEN</div></div><p>The historical record establishes CIA relationships with journalists and covert media activity. It does not, on the evidence reviewed, establish centralized control of the entire American press or prove such control exists today.</p><div class="case-anatomy"><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>VERIFIED</strong><span>Documented CIA-journalist relationships and covert media activity.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>NOT ESTABLISHED</strong><span>Total centralized control of the American press.</span></div><div class="anatomy-item"><strong>WHY IT MATTERS</strong><span>The narrow documented fact and the sweeping viral claim are not interchangeable.</span></div></div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000004.php">OPEN EVIDENCE FILE →</a></p></article></div></section><section class="section" id="trials"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">CASE INDEX // PUBLISHED & OPEN</div><h2>Evidence Files</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">PU-TOT-000003</div><h2>Who was Jesus — before religion told us who he was?</h2></div><div class="status">OPEN</div></div><p>The surviving early evidence strongly supports a historical first-century Jesus behind the Christian movement, while supernatural claims require a separate evidentiary trial.</p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000003.php">Examine File</a></article><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000001</div><h2>Does God individually cause or permit every bad thing?</h2></div><div class="status">PROVISIONAL</div></div><p>The evidence does not require the conclusion that every harmful event is individually caused or separately permitted by God. The opposite absolute also outruns the evidence.</p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000001.php">Examine File</a></article><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000002</div><h2>Did Jesus teach the modern Romans Road / sinner's prayer?</h2></div><div class="status">OPEN</div></div><p>A familiar evangelical salvation formula goes on trial against Jesus' recorded teaching, Romans itself, conversion history, and its strongest defense.</p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000002.php">Examine File</a></article></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE LAB // RELEASE 16</div><h2>Build the claim map before choosing a verdict.</h2><p>Turn one precise claim into competing hypotheses, source tests, provenance questions, counterevidence, and explicit unknowns.</p><div class="finding"><strong>Privacy boundary:</strong> no account, no automatic submission, and no hidden model call. Source Sweep sends claim-derived queries only after you start it and shows provider failures.</div><a class="button" href="/truth/lab/">OPEN EVIDENCE LAB →</a></article><aside class="card"><div class="eyebrow">THE TRUST-WORTHY METHOD</div><h2>Evidence before allegiance.</h2><ul class="rules"><li>Trace toward primary and earliest accessible evidence.</li><li>Seek the strongest credible counterevidence.</li><li>Separate independent corroboration from repetition.</li><li>Examine motive, money and power without pretending motive is proof.</li><li>Label fact, inference, uncertainty and opinion distinctly.</li><li>Revise the finding when better evidence wins.</li></ul><div class="judge">YOU BE THE JUDGE.<small>TRUST-WORTHY // PROJECT UNVEILED</small></div></aside></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap"><strong>TRUST-WORTHY EVIDENCE DESK</strong> · Project Unveiled · Question everything. Inspect the evidence.</div></footer><script>document.getElementById("questionOpenedAt").value=Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);</script></body></html>
